"literature_wall","q":152,"quote":"The literature is significant – Bjorn et al. 2022; Brander et al. 2018; Gillenwater et al. 2014; Hamburger 2019; Langer et al. 2024; and Mulder & Zomer 2016 – and underlines the importance of implementing fundamental revisions.","respondent_id":982,"title":"An energy supplier assembles a six-paper literature wall","verified":true},{"attribution":"Technische Universität München — Academia/research, Germany","key":"both_sides_cited","q":148,"quote":"References:\nBjørn, A., Gebara, C. H., & Brander, M. (2025). Untangling deliverability, additionality and double counting related to renewable energy certificates for improved Scope 2 emissions accounting. Environmental Research Letters, 20(5).\nRiepin, I., & Brown, T. (2024). On the means, costs, and system-level impacts of 24/7 carbon-free energy procurement. Energy Strategy Reviews, 54, 101488.","respondent_id":559,"title":"A university cites both sides of the hourly-matching debate","verified":true}]}
